# No .dockerignore existed before this release-hardening pass (task 18.3 /
# Workstream A). Without it, `docker build` (context: .) sends the entire
# repo checkout to the daemon, including any locally-built `dist/` output —
# exactly the kind of stale host artifact this release effort is trying to
# eliminate — plus .git history, node_modules, and anything under
# .code-intel/ or .env* that must never enter a build context or image layer.
#
# Kept deliberately conservative: workflow markdown assets under
# code-intel/core/src/agents/workflows/**/*.md are real build inputs
# (scripts/copy-workflow-assets.mjs copies them into dist/ at build time), so
# this does NOT exclude *.md broadly — only specific non-source directories
# confirmed (by grep) to be unreferenced by any build/test script.
#
# CONFIRMED THE HARD WAY (real `docker build` run, task 6.5): a bare
# top-level pattern like `node_modules/` or `*.tsbuildinfo` only reliably
# matches at the build-context ROOT in this Docker version — it does NOT
# also match nested occurrences like `code-intel/shared/node_modules/` or
# `code-intel/shared/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`, even though the same bare-pattern
# form works for gitignore. A stale, untracked `code-intel/shared/tsconfig.
# tsbuildinfo` left over from local development leaked straight into the
# build context this way and made `tsc -b` silently report success with NO
# emitted `dist/` output (TypeScript trusted the stale incremental cache),
# which then made `code-intel/web`'s build fail loudly with `Cannot find
# module 'code-intel-shared'` — the exact class of silent-incomplete-build
# risk this whole release effort exists to close, just one directory over.
# Every pattern below that must apply at any depth now has an explicit
# `**/` form alongside the root-level one — don't remove either half.

.git/
.github/

node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Stale local build output — the image always rebuilds these from source.
# (also closes: nested per-workspace node_modules/ and *.tsbuildinfo from a
# developer's local build were leaking into the build context — see above)
dist/
dist-tests/
**/dist/
**/dist-tests/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local per-repo analysis state / secrets / env files.
.code-intel/
.env
.env.*
.npmrc

# Editor/tooling directories not needed inside the image.
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.pi/
.amp/
.playwright-mcp/

# Not referenced by any build/test script — verified via grep before adding.
openspec/
docs/
screenshots/
eval/
ref-use/
coverage/
